WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.740
"Even if you've fallen once,"

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.060
"wager your life,"

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.480
"bring back your master at all costs."

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.220
"That is what it means to be my shinobi."

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:25.980
That was our little Lord, our young prince, speaking invoking our Shinobi's code of honor and

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.240
Imploring us to find him and bring him back safely.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.740
But perhaps even more striking than our Lord's voice is our own.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.700
The Undead Slayer

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.140
"Sure, I will take it."

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:51.720
In my last video, we talked about the red sheathed second blade on Sekido's back,

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.840
something that was touted as an unlockable weapon for later in the game.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.160
And this is it. The Undead Slayer

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.440
It's almost certainly a special type of blade that's for killing immortal beings

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.380
and we'll talk about it a little bit later.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.620
At the end of the video, we hear our young Lord speak once again,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.000
and this time is talking in a sort of formal, entreating tone.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.880
"Wolf."

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.940
"Along with my blood, you must live."

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.280
So we already know that our Prince is special because of his blood.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.180
That's why the Ashina clan stole him from us in the first place.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:38.600
And when he says "Live along with my blood" he could simply be imploring us to sort of fight for both of their lives.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.140
But he could also mean it in a supernatural sense.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.900
It could literally be the blood that's keeping us alive.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.420
And From Software could be hinting at something supernatural again

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.720
That's our two lives are very intertwined.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.400
There are three other characters voiced in the trailer.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.860
The first is the woman with the red umbrella. She said,

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.620
"I have witnessed"

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.540
"Syura once before."

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.820
Syura might have a bit of a double meaning. The more conventional interpretation is

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.540
that she has witnessed a scene of great carnage once before. For example,

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.600
this could be referenced to the burning village in the intro.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.380
She could be talking about all the terrible devastation that usually follows war.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:32.420
Alternatively though, Asyura is also a type of wicked demigod in Buddhist mythology.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:39.680
Sort of a type of anti-God or demon that's often depicted get this as having six arms.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:45.560
Sound familiar? I reckon it's likely that we've signed a bit of a deal with the devil here.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.220
But moving on,

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.120
"It's been a while"

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.840
"Brat of the Owl."

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.860
This is a curious statement.
The words"it's been a while"

00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:01.840
suggests that our character has a history with this woman or at least that we've met her before.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:08.380
She calls us a brat. She's rude, but who or what is the Owl?

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.440
It could be our clan. It could be our Lord. It could be our God.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:18.280
Nobody knows, but she's not the only one who speaks mockingly to our shinobi.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.000
We also have this guy,

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.180
"Am I getting in your way?"

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.380
"Shinobi of the heir."

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:29.320
This could also be interpreted as "You would block my path, Shinobi of the heir."

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.880
And this character is insane in the trailer.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:37.820
But, can I just say both this man and our shinobi have voice actors that sound

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:44.260
so so similar to the voice actors of Guts from Berserk. And if you've watched Berserk,

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:49.040
which you really should, you'll understand how bloody fitting this is.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.600
Anyway, those were just the translations.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.800
Now let's dig into the weapons, the bosses, and the environments.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.340
We open on the burning village scene, which is something that we've seen a few times now

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.000
so it must be a pretty important story event.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:08.000
Our shinobi lies beaten on the floor and

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.860
our little Lord talks about how death should not stop us from rescuing him

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:19.640
Then we're up on our feet and we're sprinting past a flag featuring a pretty complex Kanji that

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:25.600
likely references a Kudaokami, which is a sort of dragon God

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.160
residing in the mountains or

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.260
mysterious rain dragon?

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:35.700
This valley serpent that we saw in the E3 trailer does fit the bill,

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:40.320
but with the translations I'm told, we shouldn't jump to conclusions because

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:46.400
we're missing a ton of context and our translations could be a little bit inaccurate as a result.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.580
In the next scene,

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.500
we stealth over some enemies who are sitting and poring over a map

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.640
and it's definitely worth noting that Sekiro so far

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.480
has made a big effort to make sure that their enemies are actually

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:05.280
acting like they belong in their environments. They're not just standing around most of the time.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.040
And then there's this. Wall jumping.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.720
So you could not do this in the Gamescom demo.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:17.809
So it must be one of those unlockable skills that Sekiro can develop. Added to the list.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.520
And, remember if we can endlessly jump between walls like this,

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:28.060
then that should also mean that we're able to endlessly bounce on top of enemies as well.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:32.540
Three monks walk through a tranquil sun-drenched forest,

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:38.520
which is a sort of warm setting that we haven't actually explored before in a From Software game.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:43.480
Now you can still see the sunlight filtering through as we head inside actually.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:49.160
And here, Sekiro is showing off how bloody fast is possible to block attacks in this game.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:54.980
He gets perfect blocks on every one of these by tapping the L1 button. He isn't just holding it down.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:06:00.410
This is a trick wall, which functionally will be replacing illusory walls.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.300
Except I'm sure they're used for stealth as well

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:08.880
This is followed by the woman with the red umbrella who actually peers over the cliff here.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:13.300
This gave me a bit of Patches PTSD, but that I remembered.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.240
"Wait, we don't have fall damage in Sekiro."

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:18.640
"What is Patches gonna do. He's gonna have to up his game."

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.320
And then we have Fushikiri. Undead Slayer.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.660
I'm sure most of you have played The Witcher series.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:32.580
So I bet this second blade reminds you of the second silver blade that Geralt wields in that game.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:39.220
In The Witcher, Geralt has a second silver blade that is way more effective against monster-type enemies

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:44.240
and it seems like this Undead Slayer weapon will be better against

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:48.160
unnatural maybe immortal creatures in Sekiro

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:52.000
and perhaps it'll be able to unlock special moves as well.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.420
There was actually a consumable item in the demo that I didn't talk about much.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.880
It was called Divine Confetti.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:03.580
And if you used it, you spread it around yourself and it dispelled darkness.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:09.500
But the description says that it assists in fights against ghost type enemies and

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:16.520
clearly a big thing in Sekiro is going to be stealthing around and discovering the weak points of your enemies and

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:23.840
Divine Confetti that lets you hit ghost type enemies and a second sword that allows you to hit mortal enemies is

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.500
perfectly aligned with that sort of philosophy.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.980
And now since we've gone from one weapon to two weapons, why not three?

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.120
At first glance that looks like we're wielding a spear instead of a sword,

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.219
but it's actually not a main hand weapon

00:07:38.219 --> 00:07:43.049
it's a prosthetic weapon that sort of starts off as this tiny blade on your wrist.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:49.240
But then the shaft extends, mid attack to a ridiculous length that pins a far away enemy.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.800
It pulls them up close to us and then Sekira performs an art that is called Iaido [居合道]

00:07:54.900 --> 00:08:00.700
which is sort of a smooth controlled attack where you're able to pull your sword out of its scabbard

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.160
and attack in one smooth motion.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.300
The attack itself has a sort of milky white streak to it,

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.300
and I don't really know what to make of that.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:13.340
But this guy crawling away on all fours, he wants none of it.

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:17.420
Next, the Japanese symbol for smoke and then:

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:22.360
In the Gamescom demo, there was an item called "Fistful of Ash"

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:27.960
which you could chuck at an enemy and it would basically have the same function as this red cloud.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:33.180
It allows you to re-enter stealth and it allows you to make your escape.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:36.900
And you should make no mistake this sort of execution attack

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:40.900
could be an entire new category of unlockable skills.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:47.720
I bet it's not just limited to this one. Imagine how many other types of unlockable execution skills there can be.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:53.160
And then we have this incredible cinematic scene where an old woman boss

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:57.820
dashes confidently on threads as thin as spiders silk.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.860
You can see them flashing here.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:06.600
It's worth noting that this actually takes place in the temple that we've seen a few times now.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:11.640
And this was a place that we speculated might actually be the hub world of Sekiro.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:15.640
And is anyone going to talk about how fast these enemies are attacking?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:21.860
Timing your blocks to some of these attacks is gonna be like playing osu! on max difficulty.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.120
It's pretty much a rhythm game at this point

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:30.060
And then we have the corrupted monk which shows itself so I can finally talk about it.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:34.040
This was the Gamescom boss that we weren't allowed to show you guys and

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.320
Man, this was such a good fight.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:40.200
You only see a couple of elements of the fight here, unfortunately.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.440
We see this gray mist illusion phase that you can actually

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:48.340
sort of avoid by swinging between the branches and just waiting it out.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:51.540
Here you see Sekiro doing an execution and

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:56.420
taking off one of the three health bars that the monk has.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:59.840
But what you don't see is the entire rhythm of this fight.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:05.160
The boss actually has a attack pattern that's really similar to the Dancer in Dark Souls 3.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:11.640
It's sort of relentless and flowing and it takes a really long time to wear down her posture

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:15.280
to the point where you can actually do an execution like this.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:19.260
Honestly, I think since you can die so many times in Sekiro,

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:23.800
they've balanced that out by making the boss fights really, really long.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:28.700
I wouldn't be surprised if most boss fights will long like this one is.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:32.720
To finish, a white ape with a big old blade stuck through its neck

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:36.419
throws us to the ground and the trailer ends.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.200
I can't wait.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:42.180
t before I go, I have to give special thanks to all of the translators

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.540
who have offered their help to the community in translating.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:50.380
Your skills are going to be in really high demand as we explore Sekiro.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.440
Special thanks to patrons as always.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.120
Thanks for watching and I'll see you next time.

